From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: diaaney <latte@diane.zip>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 21:37:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] rapier - 1.8 combat: rod cast plays bow twang, retrieve is
 silent

1.8.9 ItemFishingRod played random.bow (bow.ogg) at 0.5F volume
with pitch 0.4/(rand*0.4+0.8) on cast, and NOTHING on retraction.
modern replaced the cast sound with entity.fishing_bobber.throw (a
1.9+ swish) and added entity.fishing_bobber.retrieve on reel-in --
a loud tell during rod PvP that did not exist in 1.8.

ARROW_SHOOT is the same bow.ogg sound file on modern clients, and
the modern cast already used the authentic volume/pitch formula, so
only the sound event changes. retrieve sound removed entirely.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/world/item/FishingRodItem.java b/net/minecraft/world/item/FishingRodItem.java
index 70d8a1caa896665f3f88a637cab3e8ad7ea52b56..b90cd9f64b489d023b5082d5555e6d6af10501f0 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/world/item/FishingRodItem.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/world/item/FishingRodItem.java
@@ -27,16 +27,7 @@ public class FishingRodItem extends Item {
                 itemInHand.hurtAndBreak(i, player, hand.asEquipmentSlot());
             }
 
-            level.playSound(
-                null,
-                player.getX(),
-                player.getY(),
-                player.getZ(),
-                SoundEvents.FISHING_BOBBER_RETRIEVE,
-                SoundSource.NEUTRAL,
-                1.0F,
-                0.4F / (level.getRandom().nextFloat() * 0.4F + 0.8F)
-            );
+            // rapier - 1.8 combat: no retrieve sound. 1.8.9 ItemFishingRod played nothing on retraction; entity.fishing_bobber.retrieve is a 1.9+ addition and is a loud tell in rod PvP.
             itemInHand.causeUseVibration(player, GameEvent.ITEM_INTERACT_FINISH);
         } else {
             // CraftBukkit - moved down
@@ -52,12 +43,13 @@ public class FishingRodItem extends Item {
                     player.fishing = null;
                     return InteractionResult.PASS;
                 }
+                // rapier - 1.8 combat: cast plays the bow twang. 1.8.9 played "random.bow" (bow.ogg) at 0.5F with this same pitch formula; ARROW_SHOOT is that exact sound file on modern clients, while entity.fishing_bobber.throw is a 1.9+ swish that never existed in 1.8.
                 level.playSound(
                     null,
                     player.getX(),
                     player.getY(),
                     player.getZ(),
-                    SoundEvents.FISHING_BOBBER_THROW,
+                    SoundEvents.ARROW_SHOOT,
                     SoundSource.NEUTRAL,
                     0.5F,
                     0.4F / (level.getRandom().nextFloat() * 0.4F + 0.8F)
